==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 95% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
**1 [[Hippoe]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 85% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
**1 [[Hippoe]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 75% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
**1 [[Hippoe]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 65% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
**1 [[Hippoe]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Use multiple cheap meatshields like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]] or [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Samba Cat]] to defend against the Doge Darks. [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]] is good in this stage as it outranges every enemy and can easily knockback the Doge Darks. Stack up UFO Cats while attacking the base so they can quickly kill off the extra enemies that spawn before any trouble is caused by them. The Doge Dark shouldn't be a problem if you beat Chapter 3 Moon in [[Empire of Cats]].

